  "notes": "Diff-derived, never issue-derived. The issue reads as a CSS regression ('vertical bars are interrupted', 'blank white row'), but the fix at 5f360b497b adds a real DOM node: SpanTreeOffset gains an isDetailRow prop and renders <span className='SpanTreeOffset--indentGuide' data-testid='detail-row-self-guide'/> when isDetailRow && hasChildren. Verified absent at 2.16.0 (0 occurrences in the file) and present at 2.17.0, so the pair keys on a testid rather than on pixels. The seed is a three-span chain so the middle span has a child, which is what hasChildren gates on, and the plan expands that middle span exactly as the issue's steps describe. No search page is involved, so hazard H3 (view-mode divergence) does not apply."
